# Comments

For any code comment you write, edit, or review, follow `docs/COMMENTS.md`.
The prior is that a comment is worse than nothing most of the time. A
typical change adds zero.

When writing:

- Before adding a comment, name which of the six kinds in `docs/COMMENTS.md`
  it is. If you cannot, do not write it.
- A comment longer than the code under it is deleted or moved to `docs/`.
- Before finishing, delete half of the comments you added. Then reread the
  rest against the page.

When reviewing: the first question is whether the comment should exist; if
not, the finding is delete, not reword. Stale but harmless is silent.
